    <statement><p>Compute the partial derivatives:</p>
<p><m>z=\frac{3x}{\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}</m></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{x}}=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{y}}=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{3y^{2}}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{1.5}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-\frac{3xy}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{1.5}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{x}}</m> using the Quotient Rule and the Chain Rule:



<m>\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{x}}=\frac{3 \sqrt{x^2+y^2}- 3 x \frac{\partial}{\partial{x}}\sqrt{x^2+y^2}}{\left(\sqrt{x^2+y^2}\right)^2}=\frac{3\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}-3x\frac{2x}{2\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}}}{x^{2}+y^{2}}=\frac{3x^{2}+3y^{2}-3x^{2}}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{1.5}}=\frac{3y^{2}}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{1.5}}</m>



We compute <m>\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{y}}</m> using the Chain Rule:



<m>\frac{\partial{z}}{\partial{y}}=3 x \frac{\partial}{\partial{y}}\left(x^2+y^2\right)^{-1/2}=-2\cdot 1.5x\frac{1}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{1.5}}y=-\frac{3xy}{\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{1.5}}</m>





</solution>
